{%- comment -%}
  Besjaar — Shopify discount visibility (2026-09-21)

  Shows the *automatic* Shopify discount that applies to a product.

  WHY A METAFIELD AND NOT compare_at_price
  ----------------------------------------
  Shopify's Liquid storefront API exposes no discount object on `product`,
  `variant` or `collection`. Automatic discounts only become visible to Liquid
  once a line is in the cart (`line_item.discount_allocations`) or at checkout.
  `compare_at_price` is a merchandising field a merchant types on the variant —
  it is NOT a Shopify discount and is frequently set without one.

  So the authoritative discount configuration is mirrored out of the Admin API
  into the shop metafield `besjaar_discounts.active` (type: json) by
  tools/sync-shopify-discounts.mjs, and read here. Every rule still carries its
  own start/end window, which this snippet re-checks on every request, so a
  discount that expires between two syncs stops showing on its own.

  AUTOMATIC DISCOUNTS ONLY
  ------------------------
  Discount codes are deliberately never shown. A code needs the shopper to type
  it, so a struck-through price next to it would not be the price Shopify
  charges. Only discounts that Shopify applies by itself, to every shopper, with
  no minimum order and no customer restriction, get this treatment — which makes
  the discounted price shown here the price that is actually charged.

  PARAMETERS
    product  (required) the product to evaluate
    variant  (optional) the variant whose price is used; defaults to
             product.selected_or_first_available_variant
    layout   'badge'     — badge text, e.g. "-20%", for the card's badge slot
             'price'     — discounted + original price, for a card price element
             'price_now' — the discounted amount alone, e.g. "€21,55"
             'note'      — the "applied automatically at checkout" line

  Renders nothing at all when no real, currently-active automatic Shopify
  discount covers this product.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign bjd_product = product
  assign bjd_layout = layout | default: 'badge'
  assign bjd_data = shop.metafields.besjaar_discounts.active.value
  assign bjd_ready = true

  unless bjd_product
    assign bjd_ready = false
  endunless
  unless bjd_data
    assign bjd_ready = false
  endunless
  if bjd_data.enabled == false
    assign bjd_ready = false
  endif

  assign bjd_now = 'now' | date: '%s' | plus: 0

  comment
    Staleness guard. The mirror can only be as correct as its last sync: a
    discount the merchant deletes or disables in Shopify stays in the metafield
    until the next run. Rather than advertise a discount that may no longer
    exist, the whole feature switches itself off once the data is older than
    max_age_days. Set max_age_days to 0 in the metafield to disable the guard.
  endcomment
  if bjd_ready
    assign bjd_max_age_days = bjd_data.max_age_days | default: 30
    if bjd_max_age_days > 0
      assign bjd_generated = bjd_data.generated_at | default: 0
      if bjd_generated == 0
        assign bjd_ready = false
      else
        assign bjd_age = bjd_now | minus: bjd_generated
        assign bjd_max_age = bjd_max_age_days | times: 86400
        if bjd_age > bjd_max_age
          assign bjd_ready = false
        endif
      endif
    endif
  endif

  assign bjd_variant = variant
  unless bjd_variant
    assign bjd_variant = bjd_product.selected_or_first_available_variant
  endunless
  assign bjd_price = bjd_variant.price
  unless bjd_price
    assign bjd_price = bjd_product.price
  endunless

  comment
    Liquid has no null object to compare against portably, so the winning rule
    is tracked with an explicit flag rather than a blank sentinel.
  endcomment
  assign bjd_found = false
  assign bjd_best_rank = -1

  if bjd_ready and bjd_price > 0
    capture bjd_product_token
      echo '|'
      echo bjd_product.id
      echo '|'
    endcapture

    for bjd_rule in bjd_data.rules
      comment
        1. Automatic discounts only. A code is not applied unless the shopper
           types it, so it can never justify a struck-through price.
      endcomment
      unless bjd_rule.method == 'automatic'
        continue
      endunless

      comment
        2. The discount must be inside its own scheduled window right now.
      endcomment
      assign bjd_starts = bjd_rule.starts_at | default: 0
      if bjd_starts > bjd_now
        continue
      endif
      if bjd_rule.ends_at
        assign bjd_ends = bjd_rule.ends_at | plus: 0
        if bjd_ends <= bjd_now
          continue
        endif
      endif

      comment
        3. It must reach every shopper unconditionally. Anything gated on a
           customer segment, an order minimum or a quantity minimum is not true
           for a single product at its own price, so it is never advertised.
      endcomment
      unless bjd_rule.customer_eligibility == 'all'
        continue
      endunless
      assign bjd_min_subtotal = bjd_rule.min_subtotal_cents | default: 0
      if bjd_min_subtotal > 0
        continue
      endif
      assign bjd_min_quantity = bjd_rule.min_quantity | default: 0
      if bjd_min_quantity > 1
        continue
      endif

      comment
        4. It must be a per-item value. An order-level amount is spread over
           the whole order, so no single product's price can be restated.
      endcomment
      assign bjd_is_percentage = false
      if bjd_rule.value_type == 'percentage'
        assign bjd_is_percentage = true
      elsif bjd_rule.value_type == 'fixed_amount'
        unless bjd_rule.each_item == true
          continue
        endunless
      else
        continue
      endif

      comment
        5. The discount must actually cover this product, and this variant.
           Collection- and variant-scoped discounts are resolved to product ids
           at sync time.
      endcomment
      assign bjd_in_scope = false
      if bjd_rule.scope == 'all'
        assign bjd_in_scope = true
      elsif bjd_rule.product_ids contains bjd_product_token
        assign bjd_in_scope = true
      endif
      unless bjd_in_scope
        continue
      endunless

      if bjd_rule.variant_ids != ''
        capture bjd_variant_token
          echo '|'
          echo bjd_variant.id
          echo '|'
        endcapture
        unless bjd_rule.variant_ids contains bjd_variant_token
          continue
        endunless
      endif

      comment
        6. Rank on a common scale (basis points off this price) so the strongest
           automatic discount wins. Only one is ever shown.
      endcomment
      if bjd_is_percentage
        assign bjd_rank = bjd_rule.percentage_bp | plus: 0
      else
        assign bjd_rank = bjd_rule.amount_cents | times: 10000 | divided_by: bjd_price
      endif

      if bjd_rank > bjd_best_rank
        assign bjd_best_rank = bjd_rank
        assign bjd_best = bjd_rule
        assign bjd_found = true
      endif
    endfor
  endif

  comment
    The discounted price, rounded the way Shopify rounds a discount: half up, to
    the cent, on this variant's price.
  endcomment
  if bjd_found
    if bjd_best.value_type == 'percentage'
      assign bjd_cut = bjd_price | times: bjd_best.percentage_bp | plus: 5000 | divided_by: 10000
    else
      assign bjd_cut = bjd_best.amount_cents | plus: 0
    endif
    if bjd_cut > bjd_price
      assign bjd_cut = bjd_price
    endif
    if bjd_cut <= 0
      assign bjd_found = false
    endif
    assign bjd_new_price = bjd_price | minus: bjd_cut
  endif
-%}

{%- if bjd_found -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign bjd_locale = request.locale.iso_code | split: '-' | first | downcase
    case bjd_locale
      when 'nl'
        assign t_sr = 'korting, automatisch verrekend bij het afrekenen'
        assign t_note = 'Korting automatisch verrekend bij het afrekenen'
      when 'de'
        assign t_sr = 'Rabatt, wird im Checkout automatisch abgezogen'
        assign t_note = 'Rabatt wird im Checkout automatisch abgezogen'
      when 'fr'
        assign t_sr = 'de réduction, appliquée automatiquement au paiement'
        assign t_note = 'Réduction appliquée automatiquement au paiement'
      else
        assign t_sr = 'off, applied automatically at checkout'
        assign t_note = 'Discount applied automatically at checkout'
    endcase

    comment
      percentage_label is formatted by the sync (e.g. "10%", "12.5%") so Liquid
      never renders a float. Amounts go through money so they follow the shop's
      own currency format.
    endcomment
    capture bjd_value
      if bjd_best.value_type == 'percentage'
        echo bjd_best.percentage_label
      else
        echo bjd_best.amount_cents | money_without_trailing_zeros
      endif
    endcapture
    assign bjd_value = bjd_value | strip

    comment
      When the winning discount is the one a promotional campaign is built on,
      the badge carries the campaign's wording ("15% KORTING") instead of the
      plain "-15%". The value itself still comes from the Shopify discount, so
      the badge cannot advertise a percentage the discount does not give.
    endcomment
    assign bjd_campaign_badge = false
    assign bjd_campaign = bjd_data.campaign
    if bjd_campaign.enabled == true and bjd_campaign.linked == true
      capture bjd_best_token
        echo '|'
        echo bjd_best.id
        echo '|'
      endcapture
      if bjd_campaign.discount_ids contains bjd_best_token
        assign bjd_campaign_starts = bjd_campaign.starts_at | default: 0
        assign bjd_campaign_ends = bjd_campaign.ends_at | default: 0
        if bjd_campaign_starts <= bjd_now and bjd_campaign_ends > bjd_now
          assign bjd_campaign_badge = true
        endif
      endif
    endif
  -%}

  {%- case bjd_layout -%}
    {%- when 'price_now' -%}
      {{- bjd_new_price | money -}}

    {%- when 'note' -%}
      <p class="bj-discount-note">{{ t_note }}</p>

    {%- when 'price' -%}
      <span class="bj-price__now">{{ bjd_new_price | money }}</span>
      <s class="bj-price__was"><span class="besjaar-ui-visually-hidden">{{ 'besjaar_ui.product.regular_price' | t }} </span>{{ bjd_price | money }}</s>

    {%- else -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Badge text only — the card wraps it in its own badge element, so the
        discount reuses the theme's existing badge position and shape instead of
        adding a second chip over the image.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if bjd_campaign_badge -%}
        {{- bjd_value }} {{ bjd_campaign.badge_suffix }}<span class="besjaar-ui-visually-hidden">, {{ t_sr }}</span>
      {%- else -%}
        <span aria-hidden="true">-{{ bjd_value }}</span><span class="besjaar-ui-visually-hidden">{{ bjd_value }} {{ t_sr }}</span>
      {%- endif -%}
  {%- endcase -%}
{%- endif -%}
